# SEC0 Exam

Completed the SEC0 exam, finishing within 5 hours including some time away from the computer.

## Thoughts

Initially, I considered skipping this exam entirely, but I'm glad I didn't. I decided to sit it as a low stakes opportunity to familiarise myself with the Try Hack Me exam format while also validating my foundational knowledge before moving into more advanced material.

The exam itself covers core computer and cybersecurity fundamentals, and while it was fairly straightforward, it reinforced something that comes up repeatedly across beginner pathways and certifications: the importance of developing a genuine cybersecurity mindset. it's about approaching problems with the right perspective. This exam gave me a chance to put that into practice in a structured environment.

Being able to reference my notes during the exam was helpful and I am glad to be  consistent at note taking, something I'll continue to prioritise going forward.

